/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*/
FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object fvSolution; }
// VMFL010-R2 -- SINGLE-LEVER (supervisor §3 ruling 2026-09-07): the ONLY change from the
// base VMFL010 is iterative convergence, residualControl 1e-7 -> 1e-9 (linear tol 1e-11).
// The base triple N=20/40/80 is KEPT UNCHANGED (drop nothing, reposition nothing). The base
// split was textbook 2nd-order in MAGNITUDE (|d32/d21| = 0.198, cf. 0.25 for p=2) yet its
// tiny finest-level second difference (+2.958e-4) was SIGN-FLIPPED -- consistent with a
// ~1e-4 iterative/round-off perturbation. Driving the floors two orders deeper puts the
// split's iterative uncertainty far below the grid-to-grid difference so the Roache sign is
// meaningful. This DIRECTLY tests the noise diagnosis: same triple -> monotone CONVERGING if
// noise, still OSCILLATORY if genuine mesh-sensitivity. NO scheme change, NO gate change.
solvers
{
    p { solver GAMG; smoother GaussSeidel; tolerance 1e-11; relTol 0.001; }
    U { solver smoothSolver; smoother GaussSeidel; tolerance 1e-11; relTol 0.01; }
}
SIMPLE { nNonOrthogonalCorrectors 2; consistent yes;
         residualControl { p 1e-9; U 1e-9; } }
relaxationFactors { equations { U 0.9; p 0.9; } }
